From 64842ee5ba0f91b2e4fcf64c169edeaea006f2da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 15:46:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0135 -- wave-41 TAS record/replay
 (engine-side, tick-keyed)

Add a TAS (tool-assisted) input record/replay subsystem for the
real-HW iter loop. Eliminates operator-timing variability from
cross-iter perf comparison: record a canonical scenario once, replay
byte-identically across every iter binary.

Design doc: docs/internal/WAVE-41-TAS-DESIGN.md in the parent
doskutsu repo (gitignored under docs/internal/).

Architecture: engine-side, game-tick-keyed. Hook lives in run_tick()
(main.cpp:123) AFTER input_poll() refreshes the global inputs[]
array and BEFORE any game logic reads inputs[]. The hook either
snapshots inputs[] to a .TAS file (record mode) or overwrites
inputs[] from a pre-recorded .TAS file (replay mode). Game-tick
keying (not wall-clock) makes the same .TAS file work across any
fps; wave-37 35.71 fps and a future 50 fps iter both produce
byte-identical engine state from the same recording.

TSR (INT 16h hook) was considered + rejected: wall-clock keying
would diverge within seconds when fps differs between record and
replay. See WAVE-41-TAS-DESIGN.md sec. A for the full trade-off.

Four DOSKUTSU_TAS_* env vars (bare prefix, not SDL_HINT_; precedent:
DOSKUTSU_LOG_TAG at main.cpp:371):

  DOSKUTSU_TAS_RECORD=<path>          record mode; .TAS output
  DOSKUTSU_TAS_REPLAY=<path>          replay mode; .TAS input
  DOSKUTSU_TAS_PRNG_SEED=<u32>        seedrand() at boot (insurance)
  DOSKUTSU_TAS_AUTO_EXIT_TICK=<u32>   game.running=false at tick N

Default-OFF: when no DOSKUTSU_TAS_* env var is set, init() bails
early and apply_input() returns at its first guard (two pointer
checks). The binary's per-tick path is unchanged except for one
cheap predicate; behavior is bit-identical to wave-37 production.

PRNG note: NXEngine has its own deterministic LCG at misc.cpp:271
(seed * 214013L + 2531011L), not libc rand(). seedrand() is never
called in the existing tree -- seed starts at 0 and increments
deterministically. So engine randomness is ALREADY deterministic
from process-start. DOSKUTSU_TAS_PRNG_SEED is therefore a
belt-and-braces insurance, not a essential fix.

.TAS file format (binary, little-endian):

  offset  size  field
  ------- ----- -----
  0       7     magic "DTASv1\\n"
  7       1     version 0x01
  8       4     u32 LE prng_seed (echoes the env var at record time)
  12      4     u32 LE flags (reserved, 0)
  16      4     u32 LE n_events (0xFFFFFFFF = stream-mode = read until EOF)
  20      ...   events: 8 bytes each, (u32 tick, u32 mask) LE

Mask: bit i = inputs[i] per the INPUT_COUNT enum order in input.h.
Events sorted by tick; one event written only when mask changes
(coalesced). Replay uses a 1-event lookahead cache; while
pending.tick <= tick_id, applies mask + advances. The <= (not ==)
tolerates the tick-skipping case per
[[wave_38_cooperative_scheduler_starvation_is_real]] -- late-fire
event with LOG_DEBUG narration rather than abort.

Auto-exit: TAS::should_exit(tick_id) returns true once tick_count
reaches DOSKUTSU_TAS_AUTO_EXIT_TICK; caller (run_tick) sets
game.running=false. The existing gameloop() while-predicate
(main.cpp:241) exits naturally; engine-shutdown[1..8] sequence at
main.cpp:723+ runs unchanged. No new shutdown path.

TAS::shutdown() runs BEFORE SDL_Quit so the .TAS record file is
flushed even if SDL_Quit hangs (W22-WB-D shutdown-hang precedent).

MVP excludes (deferred to a v2 TAS patch): save-file
canonicalization, joystick capture, byte-state divergence
verification, tick-skipping abort (warn-only in MVP).

Single-mechanism preservation per
[[single_lever_per_binary_or_else_attribution_impossible]]: TAS is
default-OFF instrumentation. Binary behaves byte-identical to
wave-37 with no TAS env vars; PLAY1 (no TAS) preserves the
wave-37 35.71 fps anchor; PLAY2/3 all use TAS replay (constant
across the matrix) so cross-PLAY audio-backend perf comparison
remains clean (only the audio backend differs).

Files:
  src/tas.h   -- public API (4 functions; namespace TAS)
  src/tas.cpp -- implementation (env parsing, file I/O, format)
  src/main.cpp -- hook integration in 4 places:
    - #include "tas.h"
    - TAS::init() after Logger::init (line ~376)
    - TAS::apply_input() after input_poll() (line ~125)
    - TAS::should_exit() at end of run_tick (line ~208)
    - TAS::shutdown() before SDL_Quit (line ~742)

CMakeLists.txt unchanged: src/*.cpp glob picks up tas.cpp.

Smoke gate banners (parent repo tests/run-gameplay-smoke.sh):
  "tas: (record opened|replay opened)"  -- optional
  "tas: auto-exit at tick"               -- optional
Both optional because default smoke runs without TAS env vars.

docs/BOOT.md env-var entries land in parent doskutsu repo
(not in this vendor commit) per env_vars_document_in_user_docs.
